# REQUIRES: cuda
# The solute units' lists against an independent all-pairs, all-near-images
# check of every evaluated frame (MDIR_TEMPLATE_CHECK_COVERAGE): alanine
# dipeptide in OPC under NPT and in TIP3P under NVT, PME, 2 fs, its X-H
# bonds constrained. The first evaluation is at the unconstrained input.
# Each site pair within the cutoff (f64, widened by 2^-20 of it, which
# contains the f32 predicate) must have an inner entry: a superset of the
# general path's pairs; and no entry may appear twice, nor a pair in both
# orders. A check at 1.5 times the cutoff, beyond every inner reach, must
# find pairs without one, so the check can fail; one that counts an entry
# twice must find a duplicate.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t/opc %t/tip3p %t/wide %t/twice %t/split-opc %t/split-tip3p %t/stretch
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/water_template_solute.py %S/Inputs %t/opc OPC NPT 200
# RUN: cd %t/opc && env MDIR_TEMPLATE_CHECK_COVERAGE=1 mdir run control.toml | tee run.log | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/water_template_solute.py %S/Inputs %t/tip3p TIP3P NVT 200
# RUN: cd %t/tip3p && env MDIR_TEMPLATE_CHECK_COVERAGE=1 mdir run control.toml | tee run.log | FileCheck %s
# The input wrapped per atom, as a .gro file is: the HH31-CH3 bond of ACE
# and waters on the faces are split across the cell, so a member's raw bond
# from its anchor is not its minimum image. The reference point of the
# member must still be its anchor's, in the anchor's frame.
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/water_template_solute.py %S/Inputs %t/split-opc OPC NPT 100 --split | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SPLIT
# RUN: cd %t/split-opc && env MDIR_TEMPLATE_CHECK_COVERAGE=1 mdir run control.toml | tee run.log | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/water_template_solute.py %S/Inputs %t/split-tip3p TIP3P NVT 100 --split | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SPLIT
# RUN: cd %t/split-tip3p && env MDIR_TEMPLATE_CHECK_COVERAGE=1 mdir run control.toml | tee run.log | FileCheck %s
# A member beyond the radius at the input (HH31 a fifth away from CH3, as
# a minimization with free X-H bonds leaves it before dynamics with
# constrained ones): the first build, before any constraint, widens the
# radius by the measured distance; constrained builds hold it again.
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/water_template_solute.py %S/Inputs %t/stretch OPC NVT 100 --stretch | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=STRETCH
# RUN: cd %t/stretch && env MDIR_TEMPLATE_CHECK_COVERAGE=1 mdir run control.toml | tee run.log | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/water_template_solute.py %S/Inputs %t/wide OPC NVE 4
# RUN: cd %t/wide && env MDIR_TEMPLATE_CHECK_COVERAGE=1.5 mdir run control.toml 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=WIDE
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/water_template_solute.py %S/Inputs %t/twice OPC NVE 4
# RUN: cd %t/twice && env MDIR_TEMPLATE_CHECK_COVERAGE=duplicate mdir run control.toml 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=TWICE
# CHECK: template coverage checks {{[1-9][0-9]*}}: {{[1-9][0-9]*}} unit pairs within the cutoff, 0 without an entry, 0 duplicate entries
# SPLIT: split input: the HH31-CH3 bond and {{[1-9][0-9]*}} O-H bonds of water cross a face
# STRETCH: stretched input: the HH31-CH3 bond from 1.0900 to 1.3080 Å
# WIDE: mdrt: template coverage: units
# WIDE: template coverage checks {{[1-9][0-9]*}}: {{[1-9][0-9]*}} unit pairs within the cutoff, {{[1-9][0-9]*}} without an entry, 0 duplicate entries
# TWICE: mdrt: template coverage: entry {{[0-9a-f]+}} appears twice
# TWICE: template coverage checks {{[1-9][0-9]*}}: {{[1-9][0-9]*}} unit pairs within the cutoff, 0 without an entry, {{[1-9][0-9]*}} duplicate entries
